---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/code-block.astro';
import GuidePage from '../../layouts/guide-page.astro';
---

<GuidePage title="Svelte" lead="One store per component; spread the attributes it hands out for each part.">
  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock label="shell" code="pnpm add @nib-ui/svelte @nib-ui/css @nib-ui/tokens" />
  <p>
    Svelte 5 (5.20 or later for <code>$props.id()</code>; before that, pass an <code>id</code> of your own). Load the
    CSS as in <a href="/guides/css/">plain CSS</a> or <a href="/guides/tailwind/">Tailwind</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use">Use a component</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    label="Language.svelte"
    code={`<script>
  import { createListboxStore } from '@nib-ui/svelte/listbox';

  let { items } = $props();
  const listbox = createListboxStore({ id: $props.id(), items, defaultValue: 'vi' });
  // Options that change later (items loaded or filtered) are passed on.
  $effect(() => listbox.update({ items }));
</script>

<ul class="nib-listbox" aria-label="Language" {...$listbox.part('list')}>
  {#each items as item (item.key)}
    <li class="nib-listbox__option" {...$listbox.part('option', item.key)}>{item.label}</li>
  {/each}
</ul>`}
  />
  <p>
    Each store (<code>createListboxStore</code>, <code>createDialogStore</code>, <code>createDataGridStore</code>, …)
    holds <code>state</code> and <code>part(name, key?)</code>; read them with <code>$store</code>. Call
    <code>update(options)</code> when options change, <code>send(event)</code> to act from code, and pass{' '}
    <code>$props.id()</code> so server and client render the same ids.
  </p>
</GuidePage>
